// aadhar-counter: hosts the Counter Durable Object for aadhar-sh.
//
// Deployed BY HAND from this directory, never by Workers Builds, and always with
// `wrangler deploy`: a Durable Object lifecycle change is refused by `versions
// upload` (error 10211), and every step of the transfer is one.
//
//   bun run wrangler deploy -c counter/wrangler.jsonc --x-provision=false --x-auto-create=false
//
// THE TRANSFER IS FIVE DEPLOYS, ALTERNATING, and this file is written for the
// one it is at. CLAUDE.md "Moving Counter out" has the sequence and the
// throwaway rehearsal that measured it (no failed request, no reset count):
//   1. aadhar-sh declares Counter in `exports` (sqlite)      <- done 2026-09-29
//   2. THIS Worker: Counter "expecting-transfer"             <- done 2026-09-29
//   3. aadhar-sh: Counter "transferred", COUNTER binds here  <- site PR
//   4. THIS Worker: Counter back to plain sqlite             <- this file, now
//   5. aadhar-sh drops the class code and the tombstone      <- site PR
//
// DEPLOY THIS ONLY ONCE STEP 3 IS SERVING. Until aadhar-sh's step 3 deploy
// commits the transfer, this Worker is still waiting for the namespace, and
// what a plain `storage: "sqlite"` does to a transfer still pending was never
// measured: both rehearsals ran this step after step 3 only. The plausible
// outcome is a fresh, empty class of its own, so treat an early deploy as
// unsafe. Confirm with `bun run deploy:promote --status` that the serving
// aadhar-sh version is the step 3 build before running the command above.
{
  "name": "aadhar-counter",
  "account_id": "1c99acdb6141579023fb97d24261ea58",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  // The class runs under THIS Worker's compatibility settings once the
  // transfer commits, so they match aadhar-sh's exactly. A drift here changes
  // the runtime the odometer and the slot claims run on without touching them.
  "compatibility_date": "2026-06-01",
  "compatibility_flags": ["enable_request_signal", "new_module_registry"],
  "workers_dev": false,
  "preview_urls": false,
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  "exports": {
    "default": { "type": "worker" },
    "Counter": { "type": "durable-object", "storage": "sqlite" }
  }
}
